<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Firozpur district</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ferozepur district</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur">Firozpur</a> (Ferozepur) district is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> river along the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. The British took over the town of Firozpur in 1835 and made it a frontier base, and battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> were fought nearby at Mudki and Ferozeshah in 1845. Its lands included the former estate of the nawabs of Mamdot.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/firozpur-district.jpg" alt="Firozpur district" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RameshSharma1 · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saragarhi_Memorial_Ferozepur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
